{"title":"Career Roadmap · Imaging Supervisor","role":"Imaging Supervisor","summary":"An Imaging Supervisor manages the day-to-day technical and operational activities of a medical imaging department.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Medical Imaging Technology - MRI / CT Specialisation"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Imaging Supervisor manages the day-to-day technical and operational activities of a medical imaging department."},{"type":"p","text":"The role sits between advanced clinical imaging practice and departmental management. An Imaging Supervisor may coordinate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT"},{"text":"MRI"},{"text":"X-ray"},{"text":"Fluoroscopy"},{"text":"Mammography"},{"text":"Other imaging services depending on the institution"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Staff scheduling"},{"text":"Imaging workflow management"},{"text":"Protocol implementation"},{"text":"Quality assurance"},{"text":"Radiation and patient safety"},{"text":"Equipment coordination"},{"text":"Department documentation"},{"text":"Compliance support"},{"text":"Patient-flow management"},{"text":"Troubleshooting escalation"},{"text":"Training junior technologists"},{"text":"Coordination with radiologists, biomedical engineers and hospital management"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification note","text":"Imaging Supervisor is generally an experienced imaging-professional/management role, not an entry-level position. The strongest pathway is a recognized medical-imaging/radiography qualification → clinical experience → advanced CT/MRI expertise → supervisory responsibilities. A generic B.Sc/BPT/BOT/BMLT qualification should not automatically be treated as sufficient for an Imaging Supervisor position."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","