MRI safety policies are followed consistently."}]},{"heading":"Radiation Safety Management","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For modalities involving ionizing radiation, the supervisor helps maintain safe practices."},{"type":"h","text":"Core principles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Justification"},{"text":"Optimization"},{"text":"Dose monitoring"},{"text":"Equipment quality"},{"text":"Staff safety"},{"text":"Patient safety"},{"text":"Repeat reduction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful metrics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CTDIvol"},{"text":"DLP"},{"text":"Dose trends"},{"text":"Repeat examinations"},{"text":"Protocol compliance"},{"text":"The supervisor should work with the organization's designated radiation-safety professionals and applicable regulatory requirements."}]}]},{"heading":"Quality Assurance","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong Imaging Supervisor needs to understand quality assurance (QA)."},{"type":"h","text":"QA areas"},{"type":"h","text":"Equipment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Calibration"},{"text":"Preventive maintenance"},{"text":"Performance testing"},{"text":"Service records"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Image quality"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Resolution"},{"text":"Noise"},{"text":"Contrast"},{"text":"Artifacts"},{"text":"Positioning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Process"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Correct patient"},{"text":"Correct examination"},{"text":"Correct protocol"},{"text":"Correct documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"QA cycle"},{"type":"flow","items":["Measure","Identify Problem","Root-Cause Analysis","Corrective Action","Recheck","Continuous Improvement"]}]},{"heading":"Incident Management","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Supervisors may need to coordinate response to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient falls"},{"text":"Contrast reactions"},{"text":"Wrong-patient/wrong-study near misses"},{"text":"Equipment failures"},{"text":"MRI safety incidents"},{"text":"Radiation-related incidents"},{"text":"Image-data errors"},{"text":"Delays"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Incident workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Incident","Immediate Patient Safety","Notify Appropriate Clinical Lead","Document","Investigate","Root-Cause Analysis","Corrective / Preventive Action","Follow-Up"]}]},{"heading":"Equipment & Vendor Coordination","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Imaging departments depend on complex equipment."},{"type":"p","text":"A supervisor should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Scanner uptime"},{"text":"Preventive maintenance"},{"text":"Breakdown reporting"},{"text":"Service contracts"},{"text":"Replacement planning"},{"text":"Consumables"},{"text":"Accessories"},{"text":"Software upgrades"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Vendor coordination"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential interactions with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"OEM service engineers"},{"text":"Biomedical engineers"},{"text":"Application specialists"},{"text":"Hospital procurement"},{"text":"IT teams"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The supervisor does not need to repair advanced hardware but should be able to identify, document and escalate technical problems effectively."}]},{"heading":"Digital Imaging & Informatics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Essential systems"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PACS"},{"text":"RIS"},{"text":"HIS"},{"text":"EMR"},{"text":"DICOM"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Supervisor-level skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Worklist management"},{"text":"Workflow optimization"},{"text":"User access coordination"},{"text":"Image-routing issues"},{"text":"Data-quality checks"},{"text":"Downtime procedures"},{"text":"Digital archiving"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Imaging analytics"},{"text":"Dashboard development"},{"text":"Workflow automation"},{"text":"AI integration"},{"text":"Interoperability concepts"}]}]},{"heading":"Department Analytics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Imaging